TYPES.md §5.1, §4.1, §3.3: in a comparison with an enum operand, a bare name that is neither a
member of the enum nor a name in scope is E2102; the record holding the check is broken (§1).
-- shop/shop.canon --
package shop

local enum Rarity { common, rare, epic }

local record Item {
  id: String
  rarity: Rarity
  price: Int(0..=1_000_000)
  warn cheap_epic: not (rarity == legendary and price < 1_000) else "an epic item this cheap"
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E2102]  shop/shop.canon:9:35
  unknown name legendary

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
